# Build context for the Dockerfile (the Streamlit UI image). Allowlist: start from nothing, then let
# in only what the Dockerfile copies. Everything else stays out, including .env, .git, .venv, .claude,
# data/ (raw CSVs and every *.duckdb; the UI opens none of them), graph/, docs/, IMPLEMENTATION.md,
# PLAN.md, every run other than the two canonical ones, and all of agent/ and schema_engine/ except the two
# stdlib-only modules the UI imports. runs/r2-final/ is the Dockerfile's default CANONICAL_RUN.
*

!requirements-ui.txt
!.streamlit/config.toml
!ops/
!rag/
!agent/__init__.py
!agent/security.py
!schema_engine/__init__.py
!schema_engine/attestation.py
!cases/
!runs/r2-final/
!runs/live-final-2/
!engine/out/detector_backtest.json
!engine/out/containment_summary.json
!engine/out/proof_snapshot.json
!ui/

# Never, even inside the paths let in above.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.duckdb
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
